<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kim Gu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1876">1876</a>–<a href="/years/1949">1949</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kim Gu was a Korean independence leader who headed the Provisional Government of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-korea">Republic of Korea</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> for much of the period from the late 1920s to 1945. He organised the Korean Patriotic Organisation, whose members included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yun-bong-gil">Yun Bong-gil</a>, and created the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korean-liberation-army">Korean Liberation Army</a> in 1940. Returning home in 1945, he opposed the division of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a> and was assassinated in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seoul">Seoul</a> in 1949.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kim-gu.jpg" alt="Kim Gu" width="320" height="424" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kim_Gu_in_1949.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
